        "original_id": "520d070c-58b9-5084-92de-fab618ace445",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Blessid Union of Souls, Blue Peter\n- People: Jeff Pence, Eliot Sloan, Chris Wardman, Paul Humphrey\n- Places: Cincinnati, Ohio, Markham, Ontario, Toronto\n- Songs: \"Hey Leonardo (She Likes Me for Me)\"\n- Albums and EPs: Walking Off the Buzz, Test Patterns for Living\n- Topics: alternative rock, new wave, synthpop\n\nFacts:\n- Blue Peter is a Canadian new wave synthpop band founded in 1978 in Markham, Ontario, by Chris Wardman and Paul Humphrey.\n- Blessid Union of Souls is an American alternative rock band from Cincinnati, Ohio, formed in 1990 by friends Jeff Pence and Eliot Sloan.\n- Test Patterns for Living was the first release, an EP, by the Toronto-based new wave band Blue Peter.\n- In their heyday, Blue Peter opened for major international acts such as the Police and Simple Minds.\n- \"Hey Leonardo (She Likes Me for Me)\" is a song by Blessid Union of Souls from the band's third album, Walking Off the Buzz.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
